  "notes": "USAGE:\n{香|かお}る is an intransitive godan verb used exclusively for pleasant or agreeable scents. For bad smells, use {臭|にお}う instead.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{香|かお}っている describes an ongoing state of being fragrant.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {匂|にお}う covers a wider range of smells (both pleasant and unpleasant)\n- {香|かお}る is limited to pleasant fragrances and has a more literary or elevated feel\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {花|はな}が{香|かお}る (flowers are fragrant)\n- コーヒーが{香|かお}る (coffee smells wonderful)\n- {香|かお}り{高|たか}い (richly fragrant)\n\nThe kanji {香|かお} also appears in the noun {香|かお}り (fragrance, aroma).",
